[
  {
    "index": 1,
    "sentence": "We wish to know if there is an integer m (depending on an integer n) such that",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Read"
  },
  {
    "index": 2,
    "sentence": "m³ = 3n² + 3n + 7.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Read"
  },
  {
    "index": 3,
    "sentence": "One way to show no solution exists is to consider the equation modulo 9.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 4,
    "sentence": "Step 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Monitor"
  },
  {
    "index": 5,
    "sentence": "Find the possible values of m³ modulo 9.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 6,
    "sentence": "Examine cubes modulo 9.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 7,
    "sentence": "Let m be any integer; then its residue m modulo 9 is one of 0, 1, 2, …, 8.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 8,
    "sentence": "Calculate m³ modulo 9:\n  • If m ≡ 0 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 0³ = 0 (mod 9).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 9,
    "sentence": "• If m ≡ 1 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 1³ = 1 (mod 9).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 10,
    "sentence": "• If m ≡ 2 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 8 (mod 9) [since 2³ = 8].",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 11,
    "sentence": "• If m ≡ 3 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 27 ≡ 0 (mod 9).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 12,
    "sentence": "• If m ≡ 4 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 64, and 64 mod 9 = 64 − 63 = 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 13,
    "sentence": "• If m ≡ 5 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 125.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 14,
    "sentence": "Since 9×13 = 117, 125 − 117 = 8.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 15,
    "sentence": "• If m ≡ 6 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 216 ≡ 0 (mod 9) (because 9×24 = 216).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 16,
    "sentence": "• If m ≡ 7 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 343.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 17,
    "sentence": "Since 9×38 = 342, 343 − 342 = 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 18,
    "sentence": "• If m ≡ 8 (mod 9), then m³ ≡ 512.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 19,
    "sentence": "Since 9×56 = 504, 512 − 504 = 8.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 20,
    "sentence": "Thus the only possible residues for any cube modulo 9 are 0, 1, or 8.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 21,
    "sentence": "Step 2.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 22,
    "sentence": "Evaluate 3n² + 3n + 7 modulo 9.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 23,
    "sentence": "Notice that 3n² + 3n = 3n(n+1).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 24,
    "sentence": "Since n and n+1 are two consecutive integers, one of them is even (although we don’t need parity here); more importantly for our purpose, let’s examine this expression modulo 9 by considering n modulo 3.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 25,
    "sentence": "Case 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 26,
    "sentence": "n ≡ 0 (mod 3):\n  Then n = 3k for some integer k.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 27,
    "sentence": "We have\n   n(n+1) ≡ 0·(0+1) = 0 (mod 3)\n  Thus, 3n² + 3n ≡ 0 (mod 9) and adding 7 gives:\n   3n² + 3n + 7 ≡ 7 (mod 9).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 28,
    "sentence": "Case 2.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 29,
    "sentence": "n ≡ 1 (mod 3):\n  Then n = 3k + 1.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 30,
    "sentence": "Then\n   n(n+1) = (3k+1)(3k+2).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 31,
    "sentence": "While the exact value isn’t needed, we can compute the entire expression modulo 9:\n   First, note that 3n² + 3n = 3[(3k+1)² + (3k+1)].",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 32,
    "sentence": "However, a quicker approach is to directly substitute a small example:\n   Take n = 1: 3(1)² + 3(1) + 7 = 3 + 3 + 7 = 13.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 33,
    "sentence": "13 mod 9 = 4.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 34,
    "sentence": "So in this case, 3n² + 3n + 7 ≡ 4 (mod 9).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 35,
    "sentence": "Case 3.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 36,
    "sentence": "n ≡ 2 (mod 3):\n  Take n = 2: 3(4) + 3(2) + 7 = 12 + 6 + 7 = 25.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 37,
    "sentence": "25 mod 9 = 25 − 18 = 7.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 38,
    "sentence": "Thus, 3n² + 3n + 7 ≡ 7 (mod 9).",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Implement"
  },
  {
    "index": 39,
    "sentence": "So the only possible residues modulo 9 for the expression 3n² + 3n + 7 are either 7 or 4.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 40,
    "sentence": "Step 3.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 41,
    "sentence": "Compare the values.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Plan"
  },
  {
    "index": 42,
    "sentence": "We found:\n  • Any cube m³ (for integer m) can only be congruent to 0, 1, or 8 modulo 9.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 43,
    "sentence": "• But 3n² + 3n + 7 is always congruent to either 4 or 7 modulo 9.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 44,
    "sentence": "Since neither 4 nor 7 is in the set {0, 1, 8}, the equation",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 45,
    "sentence": "m³ = 3n² + 3n + 7",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Read"
  },
  {
    "index": 46,
    "sentence": "cannot hold for any integers m and n.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Analyze"
  },
  {
    "index": 47,
    "sentence": "Conclusion:\nThere does not exist an integer whose cube is equal to 3n² + 3n + 7 for any integer n.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Answer"
  },
  {
    "index": 48,
    "sentence": "Thus, the answer to the question is: No, there is no such integer.",
    "sentence-type": "answer",
    "human_label": "Answer"
  }
]